RECORD 7 — POWER of S4, and S4 withdrawn as uninformative
amendment to record 6, written 2026-09-02 before any ambiguous item is scored
=============================================================================

Record 6 registered a prediction that S4 would NOT flag. A registered negative is
worthless if the test could not have flagged anyway, so the power was computed
against the alternative the test exists to detect: compression IS the tail
mechanism, sigma_MAP compressed by the development slope, r drawn from the
baseline's sigma with the same rho=0.276 clustering and seed 20260813.

  POWER OF THE REGISTERED S4 AT THE 5% LEVEL
                                   vs random_walk    vs garch
    H1, compression at slope 0.32       0.049          0.059
    contrast, slope 0.15                0.049          0.055
                                   (nominal size is 0.050)

THE POWER IS THE SIZE. The test has no ability to detect compression at all, and
tightening the alternative to a slope of 0.15 does not change that.

WHY, AND IT IS NOT SUBTLE: the registered null and the compression alternative
are THE SAME DATA-GENERATING PROCESS. Both say "the baseline's sigma is the
truth, and M.A.P.'s sigma is whatever it is". Since M.A.P.'s sigma IS compressed,
the null already contains the compression it was meant to test for. The p-value
is uniform by construction and the test can only reject when the concentration
exceeds what compression itself predicts -- an alternative nobody proposed and
which has no interpretation.

APPLYING THE BAR SET IN ADVANCE: above roughly 60% power a p > 0.05 would be a
genuine null result. At 0.049 it is a foregone conclusion, satisfied about 95% of
the time whatever is true. By the standard this project has applied to every
other gate, S4 as registered is a test that cannot fire, and that is being said
NOW rather than discovered when it passes.

  S4 IS WITHDRAWN. Its result on the ambiguous band is not to be computed, and if
  computed anyway it is not to be reported as evidence in either direction. The
  outcome branches of record 6 that depend on S4 -- "both replicate",
  "exceedances concentrate but S1 does not" -- are VOID. Record 6's S1, S2 and S3
  and their predictions are UNAFFECTED and remain registered exactly as written.

CORRECTING RECORD 6'S READING OF THE DEVELOPMENT NUMBERS. Record 6 called the
null "mechanical" and said the relation "carries NO information beyond the
selection effect". That label was wrong. The null was the compression hypothesis,
so p(null <= observed) of 0.92 and 0.885 means the observed concentration sits
INSIDE what compression-drives-tails predicts, on the weak side of it. The honest
statement is: development is CONSISTENT with compression driving the tail excess
and cannot distinguish it from the alternatives. Not evidence against, and not
evidence for.

The genuinely mechanical component -- that |z_MAP| > 3 selects small sigma_MAP,
which is the numerator of the ratio -- is real and was correctly identified in
record 6. It is why the naive form against 0.5 cannot fail. Record 6 then chose a
null that removed the circularity by assuming the very thing under test, which
replaced a test that could not fail with one that could not fire.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROPOSED REPLACEMENT — not registered, for approval before the band ends
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
The defect in both S4 forms is conditioning on z, which contains sigma_MAP. A
test that never conditions on z avoids it entirely:

  Regress log|r| on log sigma_MAP and log sigma_baseline JOINTLY, on the
  ambiguous band, cluster-robust CIs on both coefficients.

  If M.A.P. used cross-sectional volatility information fully, sigma_base should
  add nothing once sigma_MAP is known, and its coefficient should be
  indistinguishable from zero. Compression predicts a POSITIVE and clearly
  non-zero coefficient on log sigma_baseline: the baseline knows something about
  which names move that M.A.P.'s sigma does not carry.

  This conditions on nothing the models produced -- |r| is the outcome -- so
  there is no shared term between the tested quantity and the selection, and no
  null that assumes the alternative. It also has an interpretable effect size
  rather than a rank percentile.

  Its power should be computed BEFORE it is registered, on the same principle
  that retired S4. I have not computed it and am not registering this.

ADR 0032 remains unchanged, as stated in record 6. Records 2 and 4 remain binding
and are untouched by this amendment.

