PART B — the combination question, recorded as SUCCESSOR, not registered
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Recorded 2026-09-02 as the successor to the retired mechanism tests.

  THE QUESTION: does a combined volatility -- some function of sigma_MAP and
  sigma_baseline -- produce better forecasts than sigma_MAP alone, judged out of
  sample by log score and CRPS?

  WHY IT REPLACES THE MECHANISM QUESTION. Records 7 and 8 retired two tests of
  "compression versus noise" for opposite reasons: S4 had no power because its
  null assumed the alternative, and the encompassing regression had 38.6% size
  because both regressors carry error. The common cause is that compression and
  noise in sigma_MAP make the SAME prediction for every statistic available here
  -- both make sigma_baseline incrementally informative about |r|. On this data
  THE MECHANISM APPEARS UNIDENTIFIABLE, and that is a property of the design, not
  a gap to be closed by a cleverer statistic.

  The decision question does not need the mechanism. Whether M.A.P.'s sigma
  under-varies because it compresses or because it is noisy, the remedy and the
  test are the same: combine, and see whether the combination scores better. It
  is answerable, it is what Phase 3 would act on, and it is well-posed under
  either mechanism.

  WHY IT IS NOT BEING REGISTERED NOW. It needs its own out-of-sample split, and
  no unspent sample is available for it:
    - the AMBIGUOUS band is committed. It is the leakage estimate (ADR 0019) and
      it now carries S1-S3 of record 6. Fitting a combination on it and judging
      the combination on it would be the overfitting the split exists to prevent.
    - the CLEAN HOLDOUT is reserved for Phase 3 under ADR 0031, spendable exactly
      once, and a committed record proves it unspent. Spending it on a
      combination weight would consume the one sample that can test the
      pre-registered calibration.
  Registering a test with nowhere valid to run it would be the same defect as a
  condition that cannot fire, arriving through the sample rather than the
  statistic.

  WHAT IT WOULD NEED: a further corpus, or a split of the ambiguous band declared
  BEFORE it is scored. Neither exists today, and inventing the second now would
  cut into the leakage estimate the band was drawn for. It is left open, named,
